          "id": "item_1",
          "type": "agent_message",
          "text": "- **High \u2014 CONNECT allowlisting does not enforce model-only destinations inside tunnels.**  \n  **Evidence:** `packages/workflow-control/src/reviewProxy.ts`, `packages/workflow-control/test/supervisedReviewCapabilities.integration.test.ts`.  \n  The proxy checks the CONNECT authority, then forwards arbitrary bytes. A client can specify an allowed authority while using a different TLS SNI/HTTP hostname inside the tunnel. Shared hosting/CDN routing can consequently reach other services. The retained probe tests rejection of `CONNECT github.com:443`, but does not test this bypass.  \n  **Proposed correction:** Enforce the actual upstream service boundary through a constrained application gateway or equivalent verified control, and add a mismatched CONNECT/SNI negative test. Until then, describe the guarantee as CONNECT-authority filtering rather than model-only egress.\n\n- **Medium \u2014 Retained source hashes do not fully identify the implementation exercised by the probes.**  \n  **Evidence:** `docs/reviews/evidence/supervised-review-capabilities.json`, `packages/workflow-control/test/supervisedReviewCapabilities.integration.test.ts`.  \n  The network probe executes `../dist/reviewProxy.js` but records the hash of `../src/reviewProxy.ts`; no supplied evidence establishes their build correspondence. The report also omits `specialistLauncher.ts`, which constructs the tested mounts, environment and Docker restrictions. Thus matching recorded hashes cannot establish that the current launcher and proxy implementation received the reported qualification.  \n  **Proposed correction:** Record the executed proxy artifact digest, launcher source digest, and reproducible build/revision provenance; regenerate the report after verifying the build. These bindings are missing from the supplied evidence."
        }
